<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akechi Mitsuhide</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1582">1582</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Akechi Mitsuhide was a Japanese general in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>. In June 1582 he turned on his lord and attacked him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honno-ji">Honnō-ji</a> temple in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, where Nobunaga died. Within two weeks <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> defeated him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-yamazaki">Battle of Yamazaki</a>, and he was killed while fleeing, clearing Hideyoshi's path to power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/akechi-mitsuhide.jpg" alt="Akechi Mitsuhide" width="320" height="679" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 投稿者がファイル作成 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Akechi_Mitsuhide2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1582 his general <b>Akechi Mitsuhide</b> attacked him at the Honno-ji temple in Kyoto, where Nobunaga died; his heir Nobutada was also killed.</blockquote><a href="/state/oda-regime">Oda regime</a></li><li><blockquote>Hideyoshi, a foot soldier's son who rose in Oda Nobunaga's service, avenged Nobunaga by defeating <b>Akechi Mitsuhide</b> at Yamazaki in 1582 and then beat Shibata Katsuie at Shizugatake in 1583.</blockquote><a href="/state/toyotomi-regime">Toyotomi regime</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Akechi Castle, in what is now <a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a>. Died in Honkyō-ji Temple, in what is now <a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=35.42,137.08&amp;year=1572" aria-label="Akechi Castle on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8017 883 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Akechi Mitsuhide"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8467 1153h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8467 1153h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=35.42,137.08&amp;year=1572">What was here in 1572? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
